          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            in an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal groupoid
            in a category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            By the logic of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} vertical categorification
            %strong
              internal
              = succeed "-group" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            or
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} internal ∞-groupoid
            may be defined as a group(oid) object internal to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullbacks"} (∞,1)-pullbacks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associativity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+laws"} unit laws
            up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence"} coherence
            laws of these homotopies up to higher homotopy, and so on.
          %p
            A
            %em group object
            in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            generalizes and unifies two familiar concepts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                it is the generalization of the notion of groupal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Stasheff
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity-space"} space
                from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                to more general
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-sheaf (∞,1)-toposes
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
                structure, up to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence"} coherent
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+categorification"} partially defined
                (see also
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping+and+delooping"} looping and delooping
                for more on this) ;
            %li
              %p
                it generalizes the notion of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
                – or rather the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
                notion of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence"} congruence
                – from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
          %p
            Of particular relevance are such group objects that define
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+objects+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+are+effective"} effective quotients
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                these are
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} deloopable
            %li
              %p
                these generalize the notion of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
            %li
              %p
                these serve to characterize
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular (∞,1)-categories
                – such as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topoi"} (∞,1)-topoi
                – as those where every such object is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+object"} effective quotient
          %p
            A
            %em groupoid object
            is then accordingly the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+categorification"} many-object
            version of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
          %p
            But notice the following. Since this is defined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            objects. For instance a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            is, externally, a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
          %p
            Also notice that if the ambient
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            %em internal groupoid objects
            then and the objects themselves is (an
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+categorification"} oid-ification
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping+and+delooping"} looping and delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            any internal group object (externally an
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connected+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} connected
            object in the
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p A groupoid object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %msub
                    %mi C
